claim:
needs:
title: Record created, updated and closed times

The format has no timestamps. Beads filters on all three and has a stale
query for work untouched recently, which is exactly what an agent supervisor
wants. pidly can only answer it with git log per ticket.

Project fields rather than header lines: they do not help answer "can I start
this?", which is what the header's fixed positions are for.

Open question is whether closed time is needed at all given the close is a
git commit, and whether updated is maintained by pidly or left to the
filesystem mtime, which is free but does not survive a clone.
